# Titles and descriptions of the commands (blueprint 10.1). Quick search and the CLI show them.

command-projects-list-title = Show projects
command-projects-list-description = Lists the registered projects with their newest scan.
command-projects-add-title = Add project
command-projects-add-description = Registers a folder or a Git repository as a project and scans it.
command-projects-rescan-title = Scan project again
command-projects-rescan-description = Scans a project again; only changed files are read if it was scanned before.
command-projects-tools-title = Check tools
command-projects-tools-description = Checks which tools level 2 needs for the languages of a project, whether they are installed and new enough, and stores the result. Starts only version queries, never project code.
command-explorer-outline-title = Show structure
command-explorer-outline-description = Lists the layers, namespaces and types of the newest scan.
command-explorer-symbol-title = Show symbol
command-explorer-symbol-description = Shows one type or member with its metrics and members.
command-search-query-title = Search symbols
command-search-query-description = Searches the names of the types and members of the newest scan.
command-status-info-title = Show status
command-status-info-description = Shows the start time and the memory of the program.
command-explorer-source-title = Show source
command-explorer-source-description = Shows the lines of the declaration of a type or member, read from the project folder.
command-usages-query-title = Show usages
command-usages-query-description = Lists who uses a symbol, what it uses and what a change of it reaches, with the certainty of each reference.
command-graph-layers-title = Show dependency map
command-graph-layers-description = Places the layers of the newest scan and the dependencies between them for the dependency map.
command-export-html-title = Export as HTML
command-export-html-description = Writes the explorer, the dependency map and the usages of the newest scan into one self-contained HTML page. The source code is not part of it.
command-credentials-list-title = Show credentials
command-credentials-list-description = Lists the credentials that Git projects log in with and whether each is stored. Never shows a secret.
command-credentials-set-title = Save credential
command-credentials-set-description = Stores or replaces the login of a Git source in the keystore of the system. The secret is only sent here and never returned.
command-credentials-delete-title = Remove credential
command-credentials-delete-description = Removes a stored login from the keystore of the system.
